diff --git a/docs/findings.md b/docs/findings.md
index 53f5a3e..b18e45b 100644
--- a/docs/findings.md
+++ b/docs/findings.md
@@ -6,4 +6,9 @@
 | RUNTIME-001 | 2025-10-28 | runtime, torch.compile, gradcheck | Gradient tests require `NANOBRAGG_DISABLE_COMPILE=1` to avoid Dynamo interference with `torch.autograd.gradcheck`. | docs/pytorch_runtime_checklist.md:26 | Active |
 | CONFORMANCE-001 | 2025-10-28 | testing, acceptance, parity | DB-AT parity and workflow profiles define canonical pytest selectors (`-k DB_AT_0XX`) and environment flag `KMP_DUPLICATE_LIB_OK=TRUE`. | docs/spec-db-conformance.md:10 | Active |
 | DXTBX-001 | 2025-10-28 | dxtbx, crystal, API | dxtbx `crystal.get_A()` returns 9-element tuple (row-major) not numpy array; reshape as `np.array(A_tuple).reshape(3,3)` to extract column vectors for MOSFLM A* injection. Panel masks built manually from `panel.get_mask()` rectangles (untrusted regions). | dbex/nanobrag_bridge.py:370, tests/dbex/test_nanobrag_smoke.py:119 | Active |
+| DIAGNOSTICS-001 | 2025-10-29 | HDF5, diagnostics, torch, metrics | Torch backend emits `/torch_diagnostics` HDF5 group with standardized metadata (masked_mse, loss_mask_coverage, n_rois, target_shape, backend) enabling reproducible parity debugging per spec-db-tracing.md workflow. | dbex/refine_one.py:80-95, docs/spec-db-tracing.md:15-60 | Active |
+| MASKING-001 | 2025-10-29 | masking, ROI, coverage, diagnostics | Loss mask coverage in Bragg peak refinement is typically <1% (e.g., 0.21% for 92 ROIs on 2527×2463 detector) reflecting sparse Bragg peak distribution; low coverage is expected and not a failure signal. | docs/spec-db-workflow.md:24-29 | Active |
+| TESTING-002 | 2025-10-29 | testing, CLI, mocking, integration | CLI integration tests use mocking to validate dispatch logic and bridge integration without external dependencies; tests verify parser contracts, backend routing, and diagnostics structure independently of simulator implementation, enabling TDD for CLI features before backend availability. | tests/dbex/test_refine_one_cli.py:1-200 | Active |
+| CONFIG-001 | 2025-10-29 | config, dxtbx, nanobrag, mapping, pitfalls | Config hydration from dxtbx to nanobrag_torch requires: (1) beam center swap (fast,slow)→(s,f) per config_crosswalk.md:29, (2) crystal A* tuple→array reshape, (3) mask polarity preservation (True→1.0, no inversion), (4) sample→source vector normalization -s0/‖s0‖, (5) unit cell angles in degrees (no conversion), (6) square pixel enforcement per spec-db-core.md:43. | dbex/nanobrag_bridge.py:120-399, docs/config_crosswalk.md:15-72 | Active |
+| TESTING-003 | 2025-10-29 | testing, selectors, compliance, documentation | Selector status transitions to Active only after `pytest --collect-only` confirms >0 tests collected; TESTING_GUIDE.md and TEST_SUITE_INDEX.md must be synchronized with collection log artifacts to prevent documentation drift and ensure discoverable selectors. | docs/TESTING_GUIDE.md:56-68, docs/development/testing_strategy.md:169-174 | Active |
 
